 emergency medicine, critical care, and laboratory animal medicine. Some seminars are useful for graduate students with interests in applied physiology and pharmacology. Speakers may be either internal or invited from other institutions. Topics include the basic sciences as they apply to anesthesiology, such as physics and engineering, anatomy and physiology, applied pharmacology, and pathophysiology. Clinically-oriented lectures\u00a0 concerning specific anesthetic techniques and species-specific differences are also given.\u00a0", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall, Spring.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "Prerequisite: VTMED 5606\u00a0or permission of instructor.", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "Enrollment limited to: third- and fourth-year veterinary students, graduate students, interns, and residents.", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "GR", "acadGroup": "VM", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}]}, "message": null, "meta": {"copyright": "Cornell University, Office of the University Registrar", "rosterDttm": "2021-09-09T19:14:03-0400", "catalogDttm": "2021-09-09T19:15:17-0400"}}